            <h3>DR Planning Checklist</h3>
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Define RTO/RPO:</strong> What downtime and data loss can you tolerate?</li>
                    <li><strong>Assess infrastructure:</strong> Multi-datacenter? Network bandwidth?</li>
                    <li><strong>Choose strategy:</strong> Backup, active-passive, or active-active?</li>
                    <li><strong>Set up monitoring:</strong> Replication lag, backup status, failover alerts</li>
                    <li><strong>Document procedures:</strong> Manual failover steps, recovery runbooks</li>
                    <li><strong>Implement backups:</strong> Full + incremental, test restoration</li>
                    <li><strong>Schedule DR drills:</strong> Monthly testing, quarterly with full failover</li>
                    <li><strong>Train team:</strong> Ensure everyone knows the procedures</li>
                    <li><strong>Automate failover:</strong> Reduce manual intervention time</li>
                    <li><strong>Review & improve:</strong> Post-disaster reviews, continuous optimization</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h4>🎯 Key Takeaways</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>DR & BC is not optional - plan for failures</li>
                    <li>Choose strategy based on RTO/RPO requirements and budget</li>
                    <li>Active-passive replication is ideal for most ClickHouse deployments</li>
                    <li>Multi-datacenter setup provides geographic resilience</li>
                    <li>Regular testing (monthly drills) ensures readiness</li>
                    <li>Monitoring and alerting are critical for early detection</li>
                    <li>Automate failover to minimize downtime and human error</li>
                    <li>Data consistency verification must be part of DR procedures</li>
                    <li>Plan for bandwidth: geo-replication requires network optimization</li>
                    <li>Compliance & SLAs drive your DR investment</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

